://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119722.patch","merged_at":"2026-05-25T17:56:41Z"},"body":"Based on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117281#issuecomment-4312364218\r\n\r\nPartially reverting https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117281 (my old PR) out of regret:\r\n- `==` and `!=` operators now uses more laymen terms.\r\n- Removes unnecessary `[b] [/b]`.\r\n- ~~`bool` only has two possible values, so stating \"equal\" and \"not equal\" should be intuitive enough. See [`int ==`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/classes/class_int.html#class-int-operator-eq-int).~~\r\n\r\nOther changes:\r\n- Adds missing \"s\" to verbs.\r\n- Replaces `boolean values` with `[bool]` in method/operator descriptions.\r\n- ~~Capitalises `Boolean`, as it is a name, and more commonly used than `boolean`. [(source)](https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/4481/should-the-word-boolean-be-capitalized)~~\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confus